> Hi @jdic, this is expected, as Edge Runtimes are only supported via the [`driverAdapters`](https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/overview/databases/database-drivers) preview feature (driven by #21394), which allows you to plug in JS database drivers rather than the Rust drivers embedded in Prisma's Query Engine.
> 
> The databases providers currently supported are `sqlite`, `postgresql`, and `mysql` (PlanetScale / Vitess). I see you're using `mongodb`, for which we have no current plans.
> 
> Would you consider closing this issue in favor of a new one titled e.g. "Request: support `mongodb` driverAdapters"? Thanks!

thanks for answering, I had the problem when using `Auth.js`, I separated the logic to save the sessions in the browser using `jwt` and not in the database as I did before (that's when I got the edge runtime error).

If anyone comes across this same situation with `Auth.js`, here is the solution:

```ts
// auth.config.ts
export const authConfig: NextAuthConfig =
{
  providers: ...providers,
  callbacks: ...callbacks
}

```

```ts
import NextAuth, { NextAuthConfig } from 'next-auth'
import { PrismaAdapter } from '@auth/prisma-adapter'
import { authConfig } from '../auth.config'
import { prisma } from '@/prisma'

const _authConfig: NextAuthConfig =
{
  adapter: PrismaAdapter(prisma),
  session:
  {
    strategy: 'jwt'
  },
  ...authConfig
}

export const { handlers, signIn, signOut, auth } = NextAuth(_authConfig)

```

I had the same problem using mysql, Auth.js, and Next.js default installation docs. Changing the session strategy to jwt solved it! Thank you!

`session:
  {
    strategy: 'jwt'
  }`

